# 🌙 WanaagPlus

### Race Toward All That Is Good

**WanaagPlus** is a good-deeds competition platform designed to inspire Muslims to strengthen their daily worship, remain consistent in dhikr, and encourage one another to perform good deeds through friendly competition and community engagement.

Inspired by the Quranic principle:

> **فَاسْتَبِقُوا الْخَيْرَاتِ**
>
> *“So race to all that is good.”*

Our mission is to make good deeds a consistent part of everyday life by combining personal progress tracking, daily challenges, and community-driven motivation.

---

## ✨ Key Features

- **📿 Digital Tasbih Counter** — Count daily dhikr and build consistent remembrance habits.
- **⭐ Points System** — Earn points through dhikr and supported good-deed activities.
- **🏆 Daily Competition** — Participate in friendly competitions that encourage positive actions.
- **🥇 Top 10 Leaderboard** — Recognize the ten highest-ranked participants each day.
- **🔄 Daily Rankings** — Reset daily competition rankings to give participants a fresh opportunity.
- **📈 Progress Tracking** — Monitor daily activity and personal achievements.
- **🔔 Motivation & Reminders** — Encourage consistency in worship and good deeds.

## 🎯 Project Purpose

WanaagPlus aims to:

- Encourage Muslims to remain consistent in dhikr and worship.
- Promote healthy competition in performing good deeds.
- Help users track their daily progress and achievements.
- Build a supportive community centered on faith, motivation, and positive action.

## 🛠️ Technology Stack

WanaagPlus is built using modern technologies designed to support a maintainable and scalable application.

| Layer | Technology |
|---|---|
| Frontend | Next.js |
| Programming Language | TypeScript |
| Backend | NestJS |
| Database | PostgreSQL |
| ORM | Prisma |

## 🏗️ Architecture

The application follows a frontend-and-backend architecture:

- **Frontend:** Next.js and TypeScript provide the user interface.
- **Backend:** NestJS handles application logic and API development.
- **Database:** PostgreSQL stores application data.
- **ORM:** Prisma provides type-safe database access and data management.

## 🚀 Getting Started

Follow these steps to set up the project locally.

### Prerequisites

Make sure you have the following installed:

- [Node.js](https://nodejs.org/)
- [npm](https://www.npmjs.com/)
- [PostgreSQL](https://www.postgresql.org/)
- [Git](https://git-scm.com/)

### 1. Clone the Repository

```bash
git clone <YOUR_REPOSITORY_URL>
cd WanaagPlus
```

Replace `<YOUR_REPOSITORY_URL>` with your Git repository URL.

### 2. Install Dependencies

Install dependencies separately for the frontend and backend, depending on your project structure.

```bash
# Backend
cd backend
npm install
```

```bash
# Frontend
cd ../frontend
npm install
```

> Adjust the folder names if your repository uses a different structure.

### 3. Configure Environment Variables

Create a `.env` file in the appropriate application directory and configure the required environment variables.

Example:

```env
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@localhost:5432/wanaagplus?schema=public"
```

Replace the placeholder credentials with your local PostgreSQL configuration. Add other variables required by your application.

**Security:** Never commit real credentials, API keys, or secrets to GitHub.

### 4. Set Up the Database

Run the Prisma commands configured for your backend:

```bash
npx prisma generate
npx prisma migrate dev
```

Ensure PostgreSQL is running and your database connection is configured correctly before running migrations.

### 5. Run the Application

Start the backend and frontend using the development scripts defined in their respective `package.json` files.

For example:

```bash
# In the backend directory
npm run start:dev
```

```bash
# In the frontend directory
npm run dev
```

Check your terminal output for the local URLs and any configuration errors.

## 🗺️ Project Vision

WanaagPlus aspires to become a platform where Muslims can encourage one another to build lasting habits of worship and good deeds.

Through daily participation, meaningful progress tracking, and positive community engagement, the platform seeks to make doing good a consistent and rewarding part of everyday life.

